  "key": "SFCC-820",
  "summary": "search/section-header-container",
  "description": "As a Developer, I want a reusable `search/section-header-container` React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it can render a section header above search results in `search-open`, supporting both a simple heading and a sub-navigation menu layout.\n\n----\n\nThe component renders a section header that varies based on the `type` prop of its `search/header` child. When type=Heading, it displays a simple heading. When type=Sub-Navigation Menu, it renders a horizontal navigation bar with toggleable labels and overflow controls. It does not own navigation logic or label content — these are passed as props from the parent.\n\n*Props in scope:*\n\n|**Prop**|**Values**|**Notes**|\n|---|---|---|\n|size (container)|Desktop, Mobile, Tablet|Controls layout breakpoint of the container|\n|type|Heading, Sub-Navigation Menu|Controls which header variant is rendered|\n|size (header)|Desktop, Mobile|Controls layout breakpoint of the search/header child|\n|showHeader|true, false|Toggles the heading element; applies to both types|\n|showSubNavigation|true, false|Toggles the entire label row; Sub-Navigation Menu only|\n|showLabel3|true, false|Toggles third nav label when sub-navigation is visible; Sub-Navigation Menu only|\n|showLabel4|true, false|Toggles fourth nav label when sub-navigation is visible; Sub-Navigation Menu only|\n|showLabel5|true, false|Toggles fifth nav label when sub-navigation is visible; Sub-Navigation Menu only|\n|showOverflowRight|true, false|Toggles right overflow indicator; Sub-Navigation Menu only|\n|showOverflowLeft|true, false|Toggles left overflow indicator; Sub-Navigation Menu only|",
