  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "Type = Heading\n\n# Given type=Heading, when the component renders, then a heading element is displayed matching the Figma spec.\n# Given type=Heading and showHeader=true, when the component renders, then the heading is visible.\n# Given type=Heading and showHeader=false, when the component renders, then no heading is displayed.\n\nType = Sub-Navigation Menu\n\n# Given type=Sub-Navigation Menu, when the component renders, then a horizontal navigation bar is displayed with Filters and Sort controls on the right.\n# Given type=Sub-Navigation Menu and showSubNavigation=true, when the component renders, then the label row is visible.\n# Given type=Sub-Navigation Menu and showSubNavigation=false, when the component renders, then no labels are displayed and only Filters and Sort controls remain.\n# Given showSubNavigation=true and showLabel3=true, when the component renders, then the third navigation label is visible.\n# Given showSubNavigation=true and showLabel4=true, when the component renders, then the fourth navigation label is visible.\n# Given showSubNavigation=true and showLabel5=true, when the component renders, then the fifth navigation label is visible.\n# Given showSubNavigation=true and showLabel3, showLabel4, showLabel5 are all false, when the component renders, then only the base two labels are displayed.\n# Given type=Sub-Navigation Menu and showOverflowRight=true, when the component renders, then a right overflow indicator is visible.\n# Given type=Sub-Navigation Menu and showOverflowLeft=true, when the component renders, then a left overflow indicator is visible.\n# Given type=Sub-Navigation Menu and showHeader=true, when the component renders, then the heading element is visible alongside the navigation bar.\n\nSize\n\n# Given size=Desktop, when the component renders, then the container layout matches the Desktop Figma spec.\n# Given size=Mobile, when the component renders, then the container layout matches the Mobile Figma spec.\n# Given size=Tablet, when the component renders, then the container layout matches the Tablet Figma spec.\n\nAccessibility\n\n# Given the component is rendered, when tested against WCAG 2.1 AA criteria, then it passes with no violations.\n# Given {{type=Sub-Navigation Menu}}, when the component renders, then the navigation bar is wrapped in a {{<nav>}} element or has {{role=\"navigation\"}} with an {{aria-label}} that distinguishes it from other navigation landmarks on the page.\n# Given {{type=Heading}}, when the component renders, then the heading element uses the correct semantic heading tag (e.g. {{<h2>}}) at the appropriate level in the page hierarchy, not a styled {{<div>}}.\n# Given {{showSubNavigation=true}}, when a keyboard user navigates through the label row, then all visible labels are reachable and operable via keyboard alone.\n# Given {{showOverflowRight=true}} or {{showOverflowLeft=true}}, when the indicators render, then if they are decorative they have {{aria-hidden=\"true\"}}; if they convey that more content is available, that information is also communicated via text or {{aria-label}}.\n# Given {{type=Sub-Navigation Menu}}, when the Filters and Sort controls render, then each control has an accessible label announced by a screen reader.\n# Given a navigation label is in an active/selected state, when a screen reader reads it, then the selected state is communicated programmatically (e.g. {{aria-current=\"true\"}})."
